    "title": "Central Dakota Metropolitan Planning Organization Presents a Look at the Possible Future to Minot City Council - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago As Minot looks toward the next 25 years of growth, city leaders are turning their attention to how people move — not just by car, but by bike, bus, and on foot. At this week’s City Council meeting, the Metropolitan Planning Organization unveiled its long-range transportation plan, focused on safety, affordability, and community needs. The goal isn’t grand projects for show, but practical ones that fit the city’s budget and future. Next up: securing the council’s support to put the plan in motion. Jack Meyer with KX News has a brief report on the topic or you can watch the full presentation made to Council below. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
